# Canonical design data

* `packages/design-data/` is the source of truth for token data. `sdk/core` embeds it at compile time, so changes require `moon run sdk:codegen` and `moon run sdk:codegen-check`.
* Validate edits with `moon run design-data:validate`.
* Reuse existing registry vocabulary (fields, variants, anatomy parts) before adding new ids. Check `lifecycle.deprecatedIn` and `lifecycle.replacedBy` on legacy tokens before deciding between new vocabulary and a `name.legacyKey` pin.
* Preserve obsolete legacy names with explicit `name.legacyKey` pins instead of generalized exceptions.
* Do not change canonical values to work around exporter or tooling gaps.
* Token and registry changes are user-facing: add a changeset for `@adobe/spectrum-design-data`.
